{
  "era": "wotlk",
  "format": "living-azeroth-npc-summaries",
  "map": 619,
  "npcs": [
    {
      "entry": 29308,
      "name": "Prince Taldaram",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:29308:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:1007948beaf36d5f1a67c660",
            "source:8d46aa42ac2ffcc8595300f3",
            "source:c0b65b63ce7322a06863a2e4",
            "source:570678f1c6a3811f6300f679",
            "source:9bca75891d42f63328051607",
            "source:6a28dc79e666b9243c1190a1",
            "source:1860cdc4120bb3ce6fa94cfe"
          ],
          "text": "Prince Taldaram is a predatory presence in Ahn'kahet's Old Kingdom: he calls trespassers intruders, threatens to feast on them and speaks of drinking blood. His encounter also marks the activation of a magical sphere with the fading hum of magic, a strange pause in his hunt.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 29308
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 29309,
      "name": "Elder Nadox",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:29309:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:6ad753a1e4dba9d2190aa017",
            "source:dc353846bd80e1838b5718cc",
            "source:e4fbdef10c24376d0c435de2",
            "source:c4730bb0d2e2340af9a51000",
            "source:490e771dd31da89c730e8ff4",
            "source:e899b89ea5b2f564f79a2b63",
            "source:cbbee5dffc685ad5ce42c535"
          ],
          "text": "Elder Nadox speaks as a servant who asks an unnamed master whether his service is complete. He invokes the Lich King, yet also says the young must not go hungry; his encounter includes an emote announcing an Ahn'kahar Guardian hatching.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 29309
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 29310,
      "name": "Jedoga Shadowseeker",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:29310:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:a651996c96e3a478d7b0aa4c",
            "source:f07f35e02acc65b0be628513",
            "source:05ce1818c8b1b29724cc4a7d",
            "source:35aa548444d74b7848b85526",
            "source:82933eeb49b29bc8d52b1cd6",
            "source:a45f3c90eecf25c605a5c737",
            "source:7eeb4a26a2eacf954ae2bb7b",
            "source:f02c89910769907a8d055cdd"
          ],
          "text": "Jedoga Shadowseeker guards what she calls sacred halls, demands that a follower step forward for sacrifice, and asks Yogg-Saron for power before presenting a gift to her master. Her victory cry praises Yogg-Saron, making her devotion plain in her own words.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 29310
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 29311,
      "name": "Herald Volazj",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:29311:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:1473f64d754394f3699f83db",
            "source:b33f8175c0d30f9bc3661c71",
            "source:5f40a74a0adaaa3ab3c76053",
            "source:8c47bf065cda46263c7da434",
            "source:8ce9ec68f4de0c3815754d38"
          ],
          "text": "Herald Volazj's encounter speech in Ahn'kahet pairs an opaque, otherworldly utterance with whispers about lost souls and fear as sustenance. His threats portray a being whose world turns on hunger and terror, while his remaining speech is difficult to interpret.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 29311
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 30111,
      "name": "Twilight Worshipper",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:30111:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:a655bde83b82ba2729d6eff4",
            "source:b1dbe5c181502d29457ef733",
            "source:0647c4d41486423b8b699222"
          ],
          "text": "Twilight Worshippers are humanoids found in two areas of Ahn'kahet. In combat, this one casts Fireball.",
          "when": {
            "entry": 30111
          }
        }
      ],
      "title": ""
    },
    {
      "entry": 30279,
      "name": "Deep Crawler",
      "records": [
        {
          "authored": false,
          "id": "npc:30279:identity",
          "layer": "npc",
          "priority": 80,
          "sources": [
            "source:78235b1df9174a9b153f9c32",
